      "content": "Box breathing involves inhaling, holding, exhaling, and holding for equal durations (like 4-4-4-4), which stimulates the vagus nerve to activate the parasympathetic nervous system. This shift from \"fight or flight\" to \"rest and digest\" helps lower heart rate and significantly reduces cortisol levels to promote relaxation. Consistent practice can also improve focus and emotional regulation by training the body to respond more calmly to stress.",
