      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your body doesn't resist the technique itself, but extreme stress intensity can overwhelm the immediate calming effect, making it harder to maintain the rhythm initially. This isn't a hidden force, but rather a physiological reality where chronic arousal catches up with parasympathetic activation if the environment remains too hostile. However, even in high-stress situations, consistent practice builds resilience and lowers your overall baseline stress, allowing you to reap benefits like improved focus and emotional stability over time. Think of it as training your body's gears to engage the \"cool off\" faster, rather than trying to turn around a car moving at full speed instantly.",
      "source": "target",
